  "body": "Found in the delta read of PR #3650 (#2970). None of these can cause a wrong program.\n\n1. **Cost.** `crates/motion/src/multiaxis/rotary/gaps.rs` (about lines 85-185): the check uses a fixed grid of 48 x 72 rays, but each ray reads each facet near its station with no search structure. On a mesh with hundreds of thousands of facets this can add seconds to each generate. Add a bucket by station and angle, or reuse the support grid.\n2. **Units.** The note gives the stations in mm in an inch document too. Use the document unit.\n3. **Frame.** The stations are in the local x of the laid frame, and the angle is \"from the top of the laid bar toward its +y side\". A user cannot see that frame. Use the setup axis and a direction that the viewport shows, or the rotary angle word of the machine.\n4. **Picked faces.** With picked faces the note can say \"all the way round\" when only the picked faces are cut.\n5. **Chord samples.** `gaps.rs:41` caps the samples along one chord at 4096. A very long straight pass at a very fine step can get samples wider than the cover distance. The result is one extra clear cut or a false \"no pass reaches\" note, never a lost cut. Scale the cap with the chord length.\n6. The pin `a_keyway_is_cut_once_in_each_place` uses 0.1 mm; the filter's own \"same place\" distance is half a pass spacing. Make the pin use the filter's distance.\n",
